Spec: Host-only application declaration review

Purpose:
  Persist explicit host decisions against exact pending declarations without creating network grants.

Owns:
  ./RegistrationReview.cs

References:
  ./RegistrationStore.sdd
  /docs/adr/0009-windows-declaration-review.md
  ./JournalCapacity.sdd

Must:
  Validate schema-eight connection and attachment tables and reject missing current-schema journals.
  Include exact local visitor grants in schema validation and reserved revocation accounting; peer revocation atomically retires both publisher and visitor authority.
  Expose review only to the trusted in-process host; ordinary application RPC must not dispatch these methods.
  Bind an immutable snapshot to its store, application, pending revision, canonical manifest and decision version.
  Reject stale or cross-store decisions, including an intervening change back to identical declaration content.
  Keep the approved declaration separate from pending updates; denial of pending does not revoke prior approval.
  Increment decision versions on approval, denial and revocation; revocation clears the approved declaration.
  Increment authority epochs only on approval or revocation; denial preserves active imports, grants and streams while invalidating stale review proposals.
  Atomically retain administrator operation results with decisions, replay original results without reapplying and reject changed parameters.
  Use the existing operation quotas and fail closed with fixed errors on corrupt review or operation state.
  Expose caller-scope provenance and keyset-paged references only to the host, with a maximum page of `200` canonical unique UUIDs.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Verify durable decisions, stale rejection, migration, replay, concurrency and rollback.
